  "scenario-notes": [
    "This scenario starts with players in Seville, in the Kingdom of Castilla (mod. Spain).",
    "Seville is a long-standing crossroads. It linked the coast to the interior of the Iberian Peninsula, connected the Mediterranean to the Atlantic, and by 1500 was home to Africans, Europeans, and Indigenous Americans."
  ],

  "character-creation-notes": [
    "You are encouraged to be creative when creating your character.",
    "Although slavery exists in this world and may come up in the course of play, players may not participate in the enslavement of others. This means players may not actively enslave, purchase, sell, own, or otherwise manage enslaved people. Characters may have experience with slavery as part of their backstory, and players may interact with enslaved people in the setting, but there will be no roleplaying of enslavement.",
    "You can choose your character's gender, including cis and trans options.",
    "There were documented individuals during this period who lived as a gender different from that assigned to them at birth. One famous example is Catalina de Erauso (ca. 1585-1650), who lived much of their adult life as a man, often using the name Alonso Díaz. Eventually, Erauso received a Papal dispensation to live as a man, assuming the name Antonio de Erauso.",
    "While non-binary genders existed in some cultures of the Americas and Africa during this period, Christian Europeans, especially Spaniards, often had difficulty understanding or accounting for such gender identities. Players creating characters from cultures with non-binary genders should choose the gender identity that Europeans would have been most likely to associate with such an individual."
  ],

